# British English

Jon is English. All user-facing copy (posts, pages, excerpts, UI) is British English, not American.

- Spellings: colour, favourite, summarise, behaviour, travelling, modelling, analogue, licence (noun), practise (verb).
- Words: maths not math; holiday not vacation; mobile not cell phone; rubbish not trash; notes not bill (for money, say pound notes if needed).
- Idioms: British. Do not write pep talk, gotten, gonna, buddy, folks, reach out, double down, circle back, or similar US workplace/blog filler.
- Prefer talking you round, a load of waffle, quite, rather, whilst (Jon uses whilst) over American cheerleading.

If a US product name or quote requires American spelling, leave that string intact. Everything around it stays British.

```markdown
<!-- BAD -->
not a chatty pep talk
favorite, summarize, color
I reached out and double downed

<!-- GOOD -->
not a chatbot talking you round
favourite, summarise, colour
I got in touch
```
